+# Harborlight Volunteer Onboarding Pilot
+
+## Administrative Decision
+
+**Audience:** Harborlight's operations director and site coordinators.
+
+Harborlight should run an eight-week, in-person orientation pilot at **Riverside Pantry only**. One session should occur each week on Tuesday from 6:00 to 8:00 p.m., staffed by one volunteer coordinator and two peer mentors. Applicants must be able to register through either the web form or the volunteer office's phone-registration option.
+
+Riverside is the appropriate administrative focus because its recorded path from inquiry to first shift shows more friction than Northside's. The pilot should test whether a consistent weekly session, one accountable coordinator, and hands-on peer support can improve that path. The Week 8 figures are proposed targets, not recorded pilot results or guaranteed outcomes. [Volunteer Log] [Operations Note]
+
+## Record Synthesis
+
+From January through June, Riverside recorded 96 completed inquiries, of which 61 applicants attended orientation: a 64% attendance rate. Northside recorded a 75% rate. Among orientation attendees, 70% at Riverside completed a first shift within 14 days, compared with 81% at Northside. Riverside also took a median 5 business days to process a complete application, versus 3 business days at Northside. Taken together, the lower attendance and first-shift conversion rates and longer processing time make Riverside the clearer place to concentrate this pilot. These are recorded administrative comparisons, not evidence that the proposed design has already worked. [Volunteer Log]
+
+The feedback adds practical context. Forty-seven of 124 invited applicants responded, and 66% of those respondents preferred a weekday evening orientation. Eighteen wanted or strongly preferred phone registration, while 13 were unsure whether their application was complete or what happened next. The Tuesday evening schedule, dual registration channels, and a named coordinator respond directly to those reported needs. [Volunteer Feedback] [Operations Note]
+
+The evidence has important limitations. Staff hand-transcribed orientation sheets, and phone-in inquiry totals are missing for four weeks, so the inquiry denominator may be understated. First-shift completion includes only shifts entered in Harborlight's scheduling platform and says nothing about longer-term retention. The feedback questionnaire was voluntary and nonprobability-based; only 47 of 124 people responded, and Riverside respondents were overrepresented. The results therefore guide an administrative test but do not support organization-wide prevalence claims. [Volunteer Log] [Volunteer Feedback]
+
+## Operating Plan
+
+For each of the eight Tuesdays, the volunteer coordinator will manage the Riverside master roster, reconcile web-form and phone registrations by noon Monday, and contact applicants whose forms have missing fields. On Tuesday, the coordinator and two peer mentors will run the 6:00–8:00 p.m. in-person session. The coordinator will explain onboarding status and record attendance; the mentors will help with forms and first-shift selection. After each session, the coordinator will enter attendance and track whether each attendee completes a scheduled first shift within 14 days.
+
+The same definitions should be used every week. Attendance rate is attendees divided by registered applicants; first-shift completion is the share of attendees with a platform-recorded shift within 14 days; processing time runs from receipt of a complete application to a processed onboarding record. At Week 8, the coordinator should provide aggregate results to the operations director and site coordinators, compare them with Riverside's recorded baseline, and label the thresholds as proposed targets. [Volunteer Log] [Operations Note]
+
+## Tracking
+
+The table preserves Riverside's recorded baselines and the Operations Note's proposed Week 8 targets. Meeting a target would show administrative improvement during the pilot, not prove that the design alone caused it. [Operations Note]
+
+| Metric | Recorded baseline | Week 8 target |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Orientation attendance rate | 64% | At least 75% |
+| First-shift completion within 14 days | 70% | At least 80% |
+| Median application processing time | 5 business days | 2 business days or less |
+
+## Risks and Responses
+
+Separate web and phone streams could duplicate or omit applicants. The coordinator should use one shared roster and reconcile both streams every Monday. Incomplete application fields could still delay processing; the Monday review and pre-session contact provide time to resolve them before Tuesday. A late mentor absence could leave check-in or coaching uncovered, so the coordinator should confirm both assigned peer mentors 48 hours before each session and reassign a trained peer mentor when necessary. Finally, a widely circulated roster could expose personal details. The coordinator should retain the master roster, share only necessary session information with mentors, and report aggregate Week 8 figures. [Operations Note]
+
